WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.240
A dorsal lip moved to a new place can give a second body axis.

2
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.260
But whose cells built it?

3
00:00:10.183 --> 00:00:14.023
Grafts within one species had given extra axial structures.

4
00:00:14.603 --> 00:00:16.583
But donor and host cells look alike.

5
00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.743
So, two readings for the new neural tube.

6
00:00:20.683 --> 00:00:25.363
Self-differentiation: the graft's cells develop by their own origin, and make the

7
00:00:25.363 --> 00:00:26.363
tube themselves.

8
00:00:27.083 --> 00:00:32.103
Or induction: the graft changes the fate of its neighbours, and host cells build the

9
00:00:32.103 --> 00:00:33.103
new tube.

10
00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:34.913
The solution was colour.

11
00:00:35.913 --> 00:00:40.133
Hilde Mangold did the test in Hans Spemann's laboratory, for her doctoral thesis.

12
00:00:41.233 --> 00:00:42.753
She used two newt species.

13
00:00:43.913 --> 00:00:45.173
Cells of one carry little pigment.

14
00:00:46.153 --> 00:00:48.253
Cells of the other carry pigment granules.

15
00:00:49.217 --> 00:00:53.917
The granules stay visible in sections, so colour shows which embryo a cell came

16
00:00:53.917 --> 00:00:54.917
from.

17
00:00:55.150 --> 00:01:00.890
In 1921 and 1922, she cut a piece of dorsal lip from a pale gastrula.

18
00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:06.370
She placed it in the belly of a pigmented gastrula, in tissue that would normally

19
00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:07.370
become skin.

20
00:01:08.183 --> 00:01:09.563
Most embryos died.

21
00:01:10.463 --> 00:01:15.423
In the survivors, a second neural plate rose, folded, and closed into a second

22
00:01:15.423 --> 00:01:16.423
neural tube.

23
00:01:17.017 --> 00:01:21.477
Predict. If the graft simply grew, what colour is the new tube?

24
00:01:22.337 --> 00:01:23.437
If it changed its neighbours?

25
00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.350
If the graft grew, the tube should be pale.

26
00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:35.970
If it changed its neighbours, the tube should be pigmented.

27
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:42.180
In one embryo, most of the second tube was pigmented, with a narrow pale strip along

28
00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.180
its floor.

29
00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.010
In another, the whole tube was host tissue.

30
00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:50.630
The pale graft lay beneath it, as a notochord and nearby mesoderm.

31
00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:59.593
Host ectoderm that would have made skin had made a neural tube.

32
00:02:00.373 --> 00:02:02.333
For the tube, induction explained it.

33
00:02:03.217 --> 00:02:07.797
Induction is a change in the fate of one tissue, caused by a signal from another.

34
00:02:08.867 --> 00:02:10.427
The graft did three things.

35
00:02:11.247 --> 00:02:12.947
Its own cells became notochord.

36
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:19.310
It recruited host mesoderm into somites, blocks beside the tube that form vertebrae

37
00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:20.310
and muscle.

38
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:24.170
And it induced host ectoderm to become a neural tube.

39
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.310
Hence the name, organizer.

40
00:02:27.483 --> 00:02:31.323
The second axis formed at the graft, not along the host's own back.

41
00:02:32.283 --> 00:02:33.903
The pattern followed the source.

42
00:02:34.703 --> 00:02:37.463
So the organizer decides where neural tissue forms.

43
00:02:38.483 --> 00:02:42.303
It does not yet say how: by a go signal, or by releasing a brake.

44
00:02:45.717 --> 00:02:48.337
The responder must also be able to answer.

45
00:02:49.217 --> 00:02:50.417
That ability is competence.

46
00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:54.930
Wrap older and older ectoderm around early organizer.

47
00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:59.370
The response falls, and largely stops by the end of gastrulation.

48
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:03.640
The control: late organizer with young ectoderm.

49
00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.040
If that still works, the loss is in the responder.

50
00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:15.890
So host cells built the second neural tube, at the graft, while they could still

51
00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:16.290
answer.
